contentText:
Goldie Hawn&#8217;s first interaction with Elvis Presley was memorable, to say the least &#8212; and not just because she was in the presence of the King of Rock & Roll.

While appearing on The Jennifer Hudson Show on Tuesday (Nov. 10), the actress opened up about crossing paths with Presley while rehearsing Laugh-In many decades ago at NBC Studios. &#8220;I remember I was wearing a purple wool jumpsuit, and I went over to him and I said hi,&#8221; Hawn began.

