&#8220;He took my hair and went, &#8216;You look like a chicken that&#8217;s just been hatched,'&#8221; she said, making Jennifer Hudson&#8217;s jaw drop. &#8220;I said, &#8216;Oh, thank you.'&#8221;

A few years later, Hawn would headline a residency at the Hilton Hotel in Las Vegas, where Presley was kind enough to invite her to stay in his private suite. &#8220;He didn&#8217;t let a lot of people back there,&#8221; she recalled to Hudson. &#8220;But me and my daddy [Edward Rutledge Hawn], we stayed in his big suite. &#8230; I was there for three weeks. And I saw [Elvis] during that time and he was a precious, precious person.&#8221;

Also on the talk show, the Death Becomes Her star spoke about her new children&#8217;s book The After-School Kindness Crew (Pooch on the Loose #1) , which was published this past May. Hawn shared her passion for kids&#8217; literature with late friend and Imagination Library founder Dolly Parton, whom the Hollywood legend honored in August after the country superstar passed away at the age of 80.

&#8220;She was a ray of light!&#8221; Hawn wrote on Instagram at the time. &#8220;She was lit up like an angel, a joyful, celestial being. Dolly blessed us all for generations to come. Rest, dear Angel, and, as you said, keep the angels creating music and singing in the heavens.&#8221;

